    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement was to return `contactPreference` = `'EMAIL'` when an email is present, otherwise `'PHONE'`, on the owner returned by `/api/owners`.\n\nTwo edits, following the repo's existing conventions for derived owner fields:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `contactPreference` (read-only string) property to the `Owner` response schema, alongside the other derived fields like `membershipLevel` and `locality`. This regenerates the `OwnerDto` with the new field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression deriving the value from the owner's email, matching the style of the neighboring `bulkSignupWarning`/`membershipLevel` mappings:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \\\"EMAIL\\\" : \\\"PHONE\\\")\")\n   ```\n   Treating a blank email as absent is consistent with how the controller's `requireUniqueEmail` already treats blank emails as \"no email\".\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite report `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures.",
